# Run R (2026-11-08, user: "why does collapse happen - is it HER?" -> "HER off"):
# run Q (slurm/sac_scratch_2t_u5_orterm_idle_nb_a02.env: SAC from scratch, Town05 +
# Town01, one update every 5 env steps, off-road terminal, idle charge, arrival at any
# speed, temperature FIXED at 0.02) with HINDSIGHT RELABELLING OFF -- the only change.
#
# Why: in Q at 125k steps the HER legs were 40% of the replay and ~57% of the goal-mode
# rows, and ~93% of the goal-mode +100 arrivals (every HER leg ends at a frame the car
# itself reached 5-25 m further on its own clean path, so its goal image is always "the
# road ahead"). All three HER runs (P, P2, Q) used the goal image at 25-50k and lost it
# by 75-100k (wrong-goal gap -> 0 or below) while their evals fell (Q 26 -> 3 of 80).
# If HER teaches the critic that the goal image does not matter, R should keep its goal
# use past 75k. Goal mode now learns only from real goal episodes (+100 arrival and the
# progress shaping toward the real goal).
. "$REPO/slurm/sac_scratch_2t_u5_orterm_idle_nb_a02.env"
export HER=0
